        <title type="html"><![CDATA[Clarify grid-auto-flow column placement tracks]]></title>
        <id>https://github.com/mdn/content/pull/44355</id>
        <link href="https://github.com/mdn/content/pull/44355"/>
        <updated>2026-06-04T13:49:34.000Z</updated>
        <content type="html"><![CDATA[<img src="https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/33368817?u=80d39153e27b7d191281ed9b12cfb2b414418080&v=4" width="64" height="64" alt=""/><br/><h3 dir="auto">Summary</h3>
<ul dir="auto">
<li>clarify how the <code class="notranslate">grid-auto-flow: column</code> example uses row tracks before adding columns</li>
<li>point readers to <code class="notranslate">grid-auto-columns</code> for sizing implicit columns</li>
</ul>
<h3 dir="auto">Rationale</h3>
<p dir="auto">The issue report describes confusion when only column tracks are defined: <code class="notranslate">column</code> auto-placement creates additional implicit columns instead of wrapping items into the existing explicit columns. The note explains why the example defines rows and how implicit columns are sized.</p>
